  However, note that `dire->name` is part of the `dire` structure which is a pointer to the `buffer` (which is of fixed size). The `buffer` is allocated to hold a `struct squashfs_dir_entry` plus `SQUASHFS_NAME_LEN + 1` bytes. The `dire->size` is the length of the filename (without the null terminator). The code copies `dire->size + 1` bytes (which includes the null terminator) from `directory_table + bytes` to `dire->name`. Then it sets `dire->name[dire->size + 1] = '\0'` (which is actually one byte beyond the copied data).

